# ==============================================================================
# Project Anvil - Root
# .wp-version
#
# This file specifies the MINIMUM APPROVED MAJOR VERSION of WordPress that
# the AMI builder pipeline is allowed to deploy. This acts as a safety gate.
#
# If the latest available WordPress version from wordpress.org/core/version-check/
# has a DIFFERENT MAJOR VERSION than specified here, the AMI build pipeline
# will FAIL, requiring manual approval (i.e., updating this file) before
# proceeding with a major WordPress upgrade.
#
# Example: If this file contains '6', the pipeline will build AMIs with WP 6.x.x.
# If WP 7.x.x is released, the pipeline will fail until this file is updated to '7'.
#
# Author: Carrick Bradley
# Last Updated: 2025-09-24
# ==============================================================================

# Specify the APPROVED MAJOR VERSION for WordPress.
# Example: '6' for WordPress 6.x.x
6